SHA256: 35e5fd073dde1dfa3dfb7ac69e26da33b76034f730154714c12a070e39a8463c
SHA1: 3c2c0ccfeef5197d36281c943ec3b27ce14d8fc4
MD5sum: b37bbfef58da4710a6b50687c9809b60
Description: SkillFishOS V/F Governor - voltage and frequency control for the BC-250
 Drives the GPU clock and rail directly through the SMU instead of leaving them
 to the stock governor, holding a frequency ceiling that heat and package power
 are allowed to lower and to give back.
 .
 On a warm board the stock governor sheds clock while this one holds it: measured
 on Black Myth Wukong, +4.5 per cent on a cold board and +11 per cent on a warm
 one, at the same 84 degrees.
 .
 Shipped disabled. Enabling it takes the clock away from cyan-skillfish-governor:
 that unit is moved to /var/lib/skillfish-vf-governor/stock and masked, so the
 two cannot fight over the SMU. Nothing is deleted, and disabling this governor
 or removing this package puts the stock one back and starts it.
 .
 Climbing, it adds a configurable margin of millivolts over the measured curve
 (margine_salita, 40 by default). The curve is measured at its knots only, and a
 ceiling recovery ramp stops on the interpolated points in between, which is
 where this board was observed to hang at full load. The margin is taken off
 again by the next descent, never by a write of its own.
 .
 Both the governor and its watchdog keep a trail on disk under
 /var/lib/skillfish-vf-governor, one fsynced line a second plus a line for every
 change of operating point, ceiling move, park, signal and exit. The line for a
 change is written before the SMU is touched, so a board that stops in the middle
 of a transition still records which pair it was moving to. Read it with
 skillfish-vf-traccia. The previous run is kept alongside it as .1, so a board
 that hangs can still be read after the reboot that recovers it.
 .
 Part of SkillFishOS.

